    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`BUILD SUCCESS` \u2014 all 48 tests green, including the new Cp35.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-match (possible-duplicate) rule for `POST /api/owners`: when a new owner isn't a hard `identityKey` duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* telephone, it's still created and flagged.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added two read-only fields to the `Owner` schema: `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32). These regenerate into `OwnerDto` at build time and map by name via MapStruct (no mapper change needed).\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added persisted `@Column` fields `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` with getters/setters, mirroring how `bulkSignupWarning` / `namesakeCount` are stored so the values survive to a later `GET`.\n\n3. **`AssignPossibleDuplicate.java`** (new function) \u2014 scans existing owners for a match on `lastName` (case-insensitive) + `postcode` with a differing normalized telephone; sets the flag and the matching id (earliest/lowest id when several match), else `false`/absent. It runs *after* `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` (so hard duplicates are already rejected 409 and never reach it) and *before* `SaveOwner` (so it isn't compared against itself).\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `assignPossibleDuplicate` step between `assignBulkSignupWarning` and `save`, under the transaction governance.\n\n5. **Schema/data** \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns to all four `schema.sql` variants (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) and appended the matching `NULL`s to the full-row `INSERT`s in hsqldb's `data.sql` (the only seed file using positional inserts that the test profile loads; h2/postgres use column-list inserts and were unaffected).\n\nThe new `Cp35Tests` passes and the full suite (48 tests) is green.",
